      "isPrerelease": false,
      "notes": "# What's new in 1.3.0\r\n## Two new AI CLI providers — five in total\r\n\r\n- Codex CLI — seeds AGENTS.md, .codex/config.toml and a build-cluster-map skill. It launches with the trust and network flags already set, so kubectl reaches your cluster on the first run with no manual setup.\r\n- Pi — seeds AGENTS.md, .pi/settings.json and a kubectl guard extension. Pi ships no permission file of its own, so AgentBridge provides a real interceptor: read-only kubectl/helm/oc commands run freely, anything else asks you first.\r\n\r\n## Bring your own model\r\n\r\nAgentBridge seeds behavior and guardrails only — it never pins a model. Pick whichever model your CLI supports.\r\n\r\n## Clearer editing and recovery\r\n\r\nThe built-in editor now highlights TOML and TypeScript, alongside the existing formats.\r\nReset restores the seeded guardrail and command files for the selected provider; the README now spells out exactly which files each provider's Reset touches, and what it leaves alone.\r\nA broken Pi guard file stops Pi from starting — Reset gets you back to a working state.\r\n\r\n## Better error messages\r\n\r\nAfter installing an update, selecting a newly added provider could fail with a raw Unsupported AI CLI provider error. You now get a plain explanation that Freelens needs a restart, instead of a message with no obvious fix."
    },
